INT. ABANDONED AQUARIUM - TUNNEL EXHIBIT - NIGHT

A glass tunnel, drained. Green slime on the walls. Dead fish skeletons lie on the sand like dropped coins. Water drips somewhere.

Four teenagers huddle in the beam of one flashlight.

KENJI MORITA (17, backpack, scared grin) holds the light. BEATRIZ "BEA" CALDERON (17, hoodie, steady) holds his sleeve. TYRELL BANKS (18, letterman jacket, loud) leads. And NOOR HAMDAN (16, glasses, camera strapped around her neck) trails behind them.

TYRELL
See? Nothing.

KENJI
It's very dark.

BEA
It's an aquarium.

NOOR
It's a dead aquarium.

A sound. A wet slap on glass above them. All four freeze. The flashlight shakes.

KENJI
What was that?

TYRELL
Nothing.

At the end of the tunnel, a shape rises from the dried sand. Tall. Dripping. Gill slits flutter along its neck.

BEA
(whispering)
Guys.

NOOR
(whispering)
Guys.

KENJI
(at the same time)
Guys?

TYRELL
(at the same time)
Run.

BEA
^Run!

They scatter. Kenji drops the flashlight. It rolls, spinning light across the walls. The shape lunges.
